invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: parse_head copies a legacy_session_id of any length the byte names
  into the 32-byte session_id array, so a 33-byte id writes one byte
  past it. RFC 9846 §4.2.2 bounds the field at 32 and srv_parser.h
  answers a longer one with decode_error; the boundary pair in
  test/srv_parser_tests.h requires 32 to parse and 33 to be refused.

--- old
    if (session_id == NULL || session_id_len > SRV_SESSION_ID_MAX) {
--- new
    if (session_id == NULL) {
